+# Epic 7 Context: Slice 7 — Juice + accessibility (the fun-test gate)
+
+<!-- Compiled from planning artifacts. Edit freely. Regenerate with compile-epic-context if planning docs change. -->
+
+## Goal
+
+This slice completes the full game's core (E1–E9): the juice pass that sets the production look, owned audio stings, and core accessibility (colorblind safety, reduced motion, scaling, captions). It is the gate slice — on exit, the fun-test playtest runs in full, both audiences explicitly (the accessibility/depth balance is the design's most delicate surface). Pass greenlights slice 8+ content scaling on this codebase; fail means iterate via the data catalogs. The gate never triggers a rebuild. Status at compile time: stories 7.1, 7.2, 7.4, and 7.5 are implemented (PRs open); 7.3 (accessibility core) is the remaining open story.
+
+## Stories
+
+- Story 7.1: Visual juice (light-canvas polish) — implemented, PR open
+- Story 7.2: Audio juice (1–2 Suno stings, cosmetic rng) — implemented, PR open
+- Story 7.3: Accessibility core (colorblind-safe, reduced-motion, scaling, captions)
+- Story 7.4: Background maps (procedural land/ocean/parks) — implemented, PR open
+- Story 7.5: Wire aesthetics (routing + junction shaping, shipped as infrastructure) — implemented, PR open
+
+## Requirements & Constraints
+
+- Color is never the sole encoder: packet types read via icon + shape; node states via icon + outline (plus pulse). Ship Deuteranopia/Protanopia/Tritanopia palette toggles.
+- Reduced-motion option: disable flagged effects (screen-edge flash, screen shake); crises stay readable via gauges + icons + captions/audio.
+- UI/gauge scaling works for small screens and low vision.
+- Every audio alert is captioned on-screen.
+- Full input parity (mouse/touch/controller) holds under every a11y mode; no input-dependent mechanics.
+- The view never perturbs the sim: reads snapshots only — no sim-state mutation, replay byte-identical, no save-format or log-version changes for presentation or settings.
+- SFX variant selection draws only from the app-owned cosmetic rng, never the sim rng.
+- Visual canon (locked): light Mini-Motorways daytime canvas — warm-cream land, soft-blue water, green parks; glowing pipes; colored packet dots; node health colors; leak spray; UI chrome with progressive disclosure, filter/focus, alerts-as-nav; camera-fit viewport so wider/taller screens reveal more map.
+- Audio: 1–2 Suno stings (crisis alert + arrival click); procedural placeholders behind the assets/audio drop-in contract.
+- Background map: deterministic + seeded from the run seed, presentation-only; terrain is low-contrast and never gates placement.
+- Wire-aesthetics machinery ships complete but OFF behind view flags (gated verdict); do not enable without a new aesthetic ruling.
+- Slice exit = the fun-test gate: run the playtest before any slice-8 work.
+
+## Technical Decisions
+
+- Sim/presentation separation is structural: the core is a pure package; only the app layer (render/ui) imports raylib; the view consumes read-only snapshot pointers plus the drained event buffer. Snapshots are SOA memcpys into ping-pong slots; the view lerps between the last two for 60 fps motion from a 20 Hz sim.
+- Golden-harness verification: T1 state-hash goldens (pure core) and T2 pixel goldens (bit-exact software renderer). Each a11y mode adds a T2 golden; presentation-only changes must leave T1 + replay byte-identical; any deliberate T2 re-bless is cause-documented.
+- No transcendentals in rendered geometry (integer math and fixed tables such as the 16-point circle; pulse phases derive from virtual time) — keeps pixels bit-exact cross-platform.
+- Audio runs through raudio (bundled in raylib); the app owns a separate cosmetic rng stream plus settings (volumes, a11y toggles) — app-side state, never in the sim or save format.
+- Palettes are data (palette.json tokens; a palcheck oracle validates them, including water/coast/park). The background map derives from a dedicated seeded stream (`splitmix64(run_seed ^ MAP_TAG)` — not the sim rng, not the cosmetic stream) and is cached in a render texture, redrawn only on resize/zoom.
+- Accessibility settings are app-owned presentation state: same seed + same commands → identical replay regardless of a11y toggles.
+
+## UX & Interaction Patterns
+
+- Triple-redundant node-state signal: color + pulse-rate + icon — with motion off, the icon and a steady ring still carry the state.
+- Nine distinct packet silhouettes (circle, rounded-square, triangle, diamond, hexagon, pill, star, tiny-square, blob) keep types distinguishable with color removed entirely; the icon is the second channel.
+- Alert/warm colors are tuned for separation in both hue and lightness; palette toggles remap them per vision type. Terrain is monochrome value texture and never a signal.
+- Filter/focus modes double as low-vision aids.
+- Paused presentation (locked): full-brightness world, no overlay, a small edge chip marks paused — must hold under all a11y modes.
+- Crisis alerts lead as the on-screen alarm tile; audio alerts always pair with an on-screen caption.
+
+## Cross-Story Dependencies
+
+- 7.3 builds on 7.1's polished view + filter/focus, 7.2's audio alerts (to caption), the intent layer from input parity (parity must hold in every a11y mode), and the pause presentation.
+- 7.4/7.5 already re-blessed the T2 goldens; 7.3's new mode goldens must not shift existing goldens (app-layer only).
+- Slice exit unblocks the fun-test playtest → slice 8+ (the six post-gate mechanics) and slice-N content; full-depth art/audio/accessibility remain post-gate backlog on this codebase.
